Bug: numbers formed by ## are recorded as symbols

The result of pasting is always classified as an identifier, so 1##0 gives the
symbol 10, and 2##e##10 gives 2e10. Fixing this breaks the passing
test_collate_const_suffix_pasting, whose expected records 42UL and 123L as
symbols; update it in the same commit. The other pasting tests (float, hex
prefix) assume this is fixed. Intermediate entries like 1##0 are kept in
expected for now; decide whether numbers need them when fixing.
